#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:8
msgid "Access boards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:10
msgid ""
"To access Mattermost Boards, select the **Product** |product-list| menu "
"in the top left corner of Mattermost, and then select **Boards** to view "
"all the boards for your team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:100
msgid ""
"Navigate between Channels, collaborative playbooks, and boards using the "
"product menu icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:12
msgid ""
"To access boards linked to a channel, select the **Toggle Linked Boards**"
" icon to the far right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:15
msgid "Link a board to a channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:17
msgid ""
"Boards can be linked to channels and accessed from the channel Apps Bar. "
"Select the **Boards** icon from the Apps Bar in a channel to open a "
"right-hand sidebar (RHS) where channel members can search for and link "
"boards to the channel. To link a board to the channel, select **Add** "
"button to open the link boards dialog and search for a board to link. "
"Channel members can only search and link boards within the team where "
"they are also board admins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:21
msgid ""
"A channel can be linked to multiple boards, but each individual board can"
" only be linked to one channel at a time. Linking the same board to "
"another channel will automatically remove the link from the previous "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:23
msgid ""
"Open the Boards Apps Bar icon, and select **Create a Board** to create a "
"new board linked to the current channel. Once a board is linked to a "
"channel, it's listed in the right-hand side of the Boards Apps Bar. "
"Linking a board to a channel automatically grants all channel members "
"access to the board, with the exception of guest accounts. Select a "
"linked board to navigate directly to the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:27
msgid ""
"All the boards previously associated with the workspace will "
"automatically appear on the right-hand side panel post-migration as you "
"upgrade to newer Boards versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:30
msgid "Unlink a board from a channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:32
msgid ""
"If you're a board admin and want to unlink a board from a channel you're "
"in, open the Boards Apps Bar, select the options |more-icon| menu and "
"select **Unlink**. Alternatively, you can open the **Share** dialog on "
"the board, open the **Role** drop-down menu next to the channel's name "
"and select **Unlink**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:16
msgid "Use the More icon to access additional message options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:35
msgid "Sidebar categories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:37
msgid ""
"You can organize your boards in the left-hand sidebar using custom "
"categories. By default, all boards will appear under the **Boards** "
"category. To manage your categories, open the |more-icon| menu next to "
"the category to create, delete, or rename a category. With the exception "
"to the default **Boards** category, all other categories can be renamed "
"or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:39
msgid ""
"After creating categories, you can move your boards to those categories "
"by opening the more |more-icon| menu next to the board and selecting "
"**Move To…** to select the category where you want the board to be moved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:41
msgid ""
"If you delete a category with boards in it, then those boards will return"
" to the default **Boards** category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:43
msgid ""
"Categories are organized per-user, so you can arrange your boards under "
"categories that make sense to you without impacting boards or categories "
"for other users. If a board is moved to a custom category, then the board"
" will appear under that category for you only. Other users who are "
"members of the board will continue to see the board in their own "
"categories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:47
msgid ""
"If you belonged to a workspace prior to v7.2, you’ll see that the "
"workspaces have been migrated to custom categories in the sidebar. All "
"boards from a workspace are listed under a category of the same name. "
"Boards from direct messages and group messages appear under the default "
"**Boards** category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:49
msgid ""
"Categories are per-user, and can be renamed or deleted by each user after"
" migration. New users won’t have default categories, and boards they join"
" will appear under the default **Boards** category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:51
msgid ""
"Boards that you create after the migration won’t be linked to a workspace"
" and will always appear under the default **Boards** category unless you "
"move or hide the boards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:54
msgid "Drag and drop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:56
msgid ""
"You can move both sidebar categories and boards and change the order of "
"both to suit your preference. You can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:58
msgid "Set the position of a board within a category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:59
msgid "Drag a board out of one category and drop it into another category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:61
msgid ""
"To do this, select and hold the cursor over the category or board name. "
"Then move the category or board around as needed. Boards moved into a "
"category are sorted to the top of the category by default unless you "
"specifically position the board before releasing the cursor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:64
msgid "Manage boards on the sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:66
msgid ""
"In addition to moving boards to other categories, from the |more-icon| "
"menu next to each board name you can perform the following actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:68
msgid ""
"**Delete board**: If you're an admin of the board, you will see an option"
" to delete the board. Deleting the board permanently removes the board "
"from the sidebar of all board members."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:69
msgid ""
"**Duplicate board**: Creates a copy of the board and all the cards on the"
" board. The duplicated board will appear under the same category as the "
"original board. Board members and comments from the original board aren't"
" migrated to the new board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:70
msgid ""
"**New template from board**: Creates a custom board template of the board"
" and all the cards on the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:71
msgid ""
"**Hide board**: Hides the board from your sidebar only. The board will "
"still remain visible on the sidebar for other board members. You can add "
"the board back to your sidebar using the search box (CMD+K/CTRL+K)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:74
msgid "Find a board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:76
msgid ""
"From the top of the boards left hand sidebar, select the **Find Boards** "
"field (CMD+K/CTRL+K) to open the board switcher, and start typing the "
"name of the board you’re looking for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:79
msgid "Team sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards.rst:81
msgid ""
"If you’re a member of multiple teams, the team sidebar will appear on the"
" left hand side of Boards. To switch teams, select any of the team icons "
"from the team sidebar."
msgstr ""

